    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6048" root="جل" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُجَلْجَلٌ</span></b>  A man <i>very excellent,</i> or <i>elegant, in
mind, manners, address, speech, person,</i> or <i>the
like; in whom is no fault,</i> or <i>vice.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  A
camel <i>that has attained his full strength.</i> (K,
TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِبِلٌ مُجَلْجَلَةٌ</span> <i>Camels having small bells,
of the kind called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُلْجُلْ</span>, <i>hung upon them.</i> (K.)

